Chapter: ProbeRecursiveGeneric
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 H3's falsifier, and the whole of it. A self-recursive type emitted without
 indirection makes zig say "depends on itself for field declared". The plug
 boxes such a type through `zig-typedef-recursive`. The question is whether
 that boxing fires when the recursive type is ALSO parameterised.

 Two types, identical in shape, differing only in whether they carry a
 parameter. If the plain one builds and the generic one does not, the defect
 is the generic case. If neither builds, it is recursion handling generally
 and H3 is misnamed.

Section: Types

  Nat = | Zed | Suc (Nat)

  Stack (a) = | Empty | Push (a) (Stack a)

Section: Cases

  nat-depth : Nat -> Integer
  nat-depth (n) = when n is Zed -> 0 is Suc (m) -> 1 + nat-depth m

  stack-depth : Stack a -> Integer
  stack-depth (s) = when s is Empty -> 0 is Push (x) (r) -> 1 + stack-depth r

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (nat-depth (Suc (Suc Zed))))
   print-line-uni (show (stack-depth (Push 1 (Push 2 Empty))))
  end
